Cooperative-timer pump in the intro-animation ISR-waited spins (e584 + FUN_1000_38cc).

Same class as patch 017: these spins wait on state the engine's INT-8 (PIT) ISR maintains, but Ghidra
folded them to bare spins with no pump.  Our host drives the engine's installed INT-8 ISR cooperatively
(native_main fist_timer_pump), so a spin that never reaches a pump site hangs.  Faithful fix: pump the
cooperative ISR inside each spin (the real ISR fires asynchronously there).
  * FUN_0000_e584 (intro/title animation player), two frame-timing waits `while ((c452 - b6e6) < b6e0)`
    on the INT-8 tick counter DGROUP:0x452 -- pump so c452 advances and the frame timer elapses.
  * FUN_1000_38cc (driver frame/vsync wait) `do { (*c40a)(); } while (CF==0)` -- pump the tick.  NB the
    real exit is CF=1 from the driver vsync-poll method c40a (DGROUP:0x40a), a driver method vector that
    is NOT yet installed (traps -> CF=0); installing it is the documented next frontier.  Asm-verified
    (e584 spin 0xe66a; 38cc 0x138cc `xchg;lcall[0x40a];jae`).
